(2317427, 320967, 19982, '<td valign="top">I like the idea presented here.  I think I''d prefer to see both eyes of each of the girls, so maybe have them positioned just slightly more to the outside.  (I''m just not a big fan of the one-eyed shots).  Also, for me, skin tones and brightness could also be improved.</td>', 'I like the idea presented here.  I think I''d prefer to see both eyes of each of the girls, so maybe have them positioned just slightly more to the outside.  (I''m just not a big fan of the one-eyed shots).  Also, for me, skin tones and brightness could also be improved.', '2006-04-17 01:55:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2317428, 320846, 48228, '<td valign="top">Sweet, and so well done.....</td>', 'Sweet, and so well done.....', '2006-04-17 01:56:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(2317429, 321973, 48228, '<td valign="top">Unusual idea here, but it works...</td>', 'Unusual idea here, but it works...', '2006-04-17 01:56:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2317432, 321939, 48228, '<td valign="top">Yes, a great portrait image.....</td>', 'Yes, a great portrait image.....', '2006-04-17 01:57:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2317434, 320337, 19982, '<td valign="top">I like the overall look and lighting on the face, but for me, the whites of the eyes have been over-whitened.</td>', 'I like the overall look and lighting on the face, but for me, the whites of the eyes have been over-whitened.', '2006-04-17 01:57:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2317443, 322016, 19982, '<td valign="top">I like the softness... except around the eyes, it feels like it has gone too soft (potentially, it may have been out of focus).  The thing that makes it feel wrong is that her right shoulder (left side of the image) appears to be very sharp, even while her eyes are blurred.  So either the camera focused on the wrong location, or the post processing softness wasn''t applied across the entire image - in which case, the best place to reduce the softness is in the eyes.</td>', 'I like the softness... except around the eyes, it feels like it has gone too soft (potentially, it may have been out of focus).  The thing that makes it feel wrong is that her right shoulder (left side of the image) appears to be very sharp, even while her eyes are blurred.  So either the camera focused on the wrong location, or the post processing softness wasn''t applied across the entire image - in which case, the best place to reduce the softness is in the eyes.', '2006-04-17 01:59:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2317448, 322001, 48228, '<td valign="top">Very sweet...</td>', 'Very sweet...', '2006-04-17 02:01:07.000000', NULL, 1),
