(2319488, 321875, 18197, '<td valign="top">Wonderful photo. Color saturation and skin tones are very good. It feels a littl heavy on sharpening. A little less would have improved the photo IMO.</td>', 'Wonderful photo. Color saturation and skin tones are very good. It feels a littl heavy on sharpening. A little less would have improved the photo IMO.', '2006-04-17 15:52:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319492, 321707, 18197, '<td valign="top">Overly post process IMO. Makes it look unnatural. Otherwise a worthy photo.</td>', 'Overly post process IMO. Makes it look unnatural. Otherwise a worthy photo.', '2006-04-17 15:54:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319498, 321410, 18197, '<td valign="top">Sharper focus would have received an additional point from me. Otherwise well composed. Well lit. Possibly a little bright on the face.</td>', 'Sharper focus would have received an additional point from me. Otherwise well composed. Well lit. Possibly a little bright on the face.', '2006-04-17 15:55:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319499, 321879, 18197, '<td valign="top">Good photo cropped to tightly IMO.</td>', 'Good photo cropped to tightly IMO.', '2006-04-17 15:56:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319502, 321227, 40667, '<td valign="top">Really like it, looks great. Feelings prettydramatic! great job!</td>', 'Really like it, looks great. Feelings prettydramatic! great job!', '2006-04-17 15:57:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319503, 321889, 18197, '<td valign="top">Fantastic photo spoiled by the lace in my opinion. Colors are superb, especially in the hair and the eyes. Composition is very good.</td>', 'Fantastic photo spoiled by the lace in my opinion. Colors are superb, especially in the hair and the eyes. Composition is very good.', '2006-04-17 15:57:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319512, 321604, 40667, '<td valign="top">Really like it! great idea! pulled it off wonderfuly!</td>', 'Really like it! great idea! pulled it off wonderfuly!', '2006-04-17 15:59:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319569, 320587, 35645, '<td valign="top">I think that what I find odd about this photo is the focus. To be a little more accurate, it''s the focus combined with the pose. The forehead, hairline, eyes and nose are crisp and well-defined, yet the mouth and jawline are not. There does not appear to be enough change in ''depth'' in the pose to cause this (the head does not seemed to be tilted down enough to cause this), so it appears to be a result of post-processing. It may indeed have been done in camera (and thus be an optical illusion), but it throws off the ''feel'' of the photo for me - it just feels inconsistent.<br/>Other than the focus issues, though, it''s quite a good shot. The pose and composition are quite good, and the skin tones are very good. I also like that the eyes look natural. The choice of background color is unusual (to me) for a male subject, but it works quite nicely.</td>', 'I think that what I find odd about this photo is the focus. To be a little more accurate, it''s the focus combined with the pose. The forehead, hairline, eyes and nose are crisp and well-defined, yet the mouth and jawline are not. There does not appear to be enough change in ''depth'' in the pose to cause this (the head does not seemed to be tilted down enough to cause this), so it appears to be a result of post-processing. It may indeed have been done in camera (and thus be an optical illusion), but it throws off the ''feel'' of the photo for me - it just feels inconsistent.Other than the focus issues, though, it''s quite a good shot. The pose and composition are quite good, and the skin tones are very good. I also like that the eyes look natural. The choice of background color is unusual (to me) for a male subject, but it works quite nicely.', '2006-04-17 16:19:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319580, 321556, 35645, '<td valign="top">I can see that the processing is intentional, and that you''re going for a particualr ''look'' with this, but I think you may have overdone it just a bit. I like seeing the texture in her hair and lips, and I would like to see just a bit more of it in her skin (as well as just a hair more color and less ''glow''). I like the pose and the expression, it''s just a bit overdone in the processing.</td>', 'I can see that the processing is intentional, and that you''re going for a particualr ''look'' with this, but I think you may have overdone it just a bit. I like seeing the texture in her hair and lips, and I would like to see just a bit more of it in her skin (as well as just a hair more color and less ''glow''). I like the pose and the expression, it''s just a bit overdone in the processing.', '2006-04-17 16:23:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319593, 320926, 15204, '<td valign="top">Very cute and emotive.  Nicely lit.  The tilt is a bit extreme for my taste. 7 from me.</td>', 'Very cute and emotive.  Nicely lit.  The tilt is a bit extreme for my taste. 7 from me.', '2006-04-17 16:25:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319598, 321936, 15204, '<td valign="top">Love the DOF and your skin tones look perfect.  THe centered composition works really well here, IMO.  It suits his level gaze.  7 from me.</td>', 'Love the DOF and your skin tones look perfect.  THe centered composition works really well here, IMO.  It suits his level gaze.  7 from me.', '2006-04-17 16:28:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319601, 321910, 15204, '<td valign="top">I love the dramatic lighting.  It creates a perfect mood for his expression.  Well done getting a catchlight into his left eye.  I think the highlights are too hot, though. 7 from me.</td>', 'I love the dramatic lighting.  It creates a perfect mood for his expression.  Well done getting a catchlight into his left eye.  I think the highlights are too hot, though. 7 from me.', '2006-04-17 16:30:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319606, 321858, 15204, '<td valign="top">Love the angle and DOF.  Having both of their eyes on a diagonal makes for a very interesting composition.  Excellent color as well.  Her face looks a little plasticky to me.</td>', 'Love the angle and DOF.  Having both of their eyes on a diagonal makes for a very interesting composition.  Excellent color as well.  Her face looks a little plasticky to me.', '2006-04-17 16:32:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319610, 321726, 32254, '<td valign="top">Another good one, would have rated higher if I hadn''t already seen the other.</td>', 'Another good one, would have rated higher if I hadn''t already seen the other.', '2006-04-17 16:32:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319616, 321898, 15204, '<td valign="top">Great lighting.  I like the motion blur in the hand, too.  I think he should have turned his head a tiny bit so that his nose doesn''t skim the plane of his cheek.  That''s a small nitpick, though.</td>', 'Great lighting.  I like the motion blur in the hand, too.  I think he should have turned his head a tiny bit so that his nose doesn''t skim the plane of his cheek.  That''s a small nitpick, though.', '2006-04-17 16:34:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319618, 321875, 15204, '<td valign="top">Nice skim lighting to bring out all the detail and character in her face.  I wish there was a catchlight in her right eye.</td>', 'Nice skim lighting to bring out all the detail and character in her face.  I wish there was a catchlight in her right eye.', '2006-04-17 16:34:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319620, 321833, 15204, '<td valign="top">Lovely colors and tones in the setting.  Her expression doesn''t seem to fit and seems awkward, though.</td>', 'Lovely colors and tones in the setting.  Her expression doesn''t seem to fit and seems awkward, though.', '2006-04-17 16:35:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319622, 321612, 15204, '<td valign="top">The skin tones seem too red on my monitor.  Nice pose and great smiles.</td>', 'The skin tones seem too red on my monitor.  Nice pose and great smiles.', '2006-04-17 16:36:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319623, 322009, 15204, '<td valign="top">A very nice moment between them.  The composition really enhances the closeness.  It looks like your main light is too low.  The light seems to come from slightly below them.  The light on the mother''s back and cheek is a little too harsh.</td>', 'A very nice moment between them.  The composition really enhances the closeness.  It looks like your main light is too low.  The light seems to come from slightly below them.  The light on the mother''s back and cheek is a little too harsh.', '2006-04-17 16:36:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319624, 321975, 35645, '<td valign="top">I like the pose, she''s cute as a button, and her outfit really works with the photo. The color and composition are quite good.<br/>The light is a little harsh. This can be avoided by either bouncing the light off of another surface (a white card or reflector) or diffusing the light (an easy way to do that is to hold a white trash bag up in front of your light).<br/>The thing that really bugs me about this, though, is the makeup. (And please don''t take offense at this - I am just stating my opinion and my reaction to this photo.) Unless she is horribly disfigured, she shouldn''t need it. I know little girls like to play dress-up and such (and they are terribly cute), but adult-style makeup on small children just really creeps me out. I''m aware that it''s a personal preference, and I''m not trying to say that you shouldn''t let her wear it, I''m just stating my feelings on it. I think the reason that it bothers me so much in this case is that with the makeup (the eye shadow in particular), she looks like she''s trying to grow up too fast, and not necessarily in a good direction. I know that that was not the intent here, and I do indeed understand that it is just a child playing ''dress-up and look pretty for the picture'', but for me it''s just a case of ''too much''. <br/>With the makeup, it''s a decent photo. But I think if you were to reshoot this without the makeup, it would be a charming picture to treasure for years to come.</td>', 'I like the pose, she''s cute as a button, and her outfit really works with the photo. The color and composition are quite good.The light is a little harsh. This can be avoided by either bouncing the light off of another surface (a white card or reflector) or diffusing the light (an easy way to do that is to hold a white trash bag up in front of your light).The thing that really bugs me about this, though, is the makeup. (And please don''t take offense at this - I am just stating my opinion and my reaction to this photo.) Unless she is horribly disfigured, she shouldn''t need it. I know little girls like to play dress-up and such (and they are terribly cute), but adult-style makeup on small children just really creeps me out. I''m aware that it''s a personal preference, and I''m not trying to say that you shouldn''t let her wear it, I''m just stating my feelings on it. I think the reason that it bothers me so much in this case is that with the makeup (the eye shadow in particular), she looks like she''s trying to grow up too fast, and not necessarily in a good direction. I know that that was not the intent here, and I do indeed understand that it is just a child playing ''dress-up and look pretty for the picture'', but for me it''s just a case of ''too much''. With the makeup, it''s a decent photo. But I think if you were to reshoot this without the makeup, it would be a charming picture to treasure for years to come.', '2006-04-17 16:36:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319633, 321271, 43434, '<td valign="top">This is lovely ... the heavy shadow in the background is distracting having her a littel further away from the wall may have lessened this distraction.</td>', 'This is lovely ... the heavy shadow in the background is distracting having her a littel further away from the wall may have lessened this distraction.', '2006-04-17 16:40:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319634, 321376, 15204, '<td valign="top">A beautiful baby!  Her skin tones seem a bit cool to me.  Nice focus and the hood is very cute.  The light is coming from below her, which is not the most flattering way to light the face.  Next time try turning her around and shooting from above her head (so she has to look up at you) instead of standing at her feet.  It helps avoid that ''up the nose'' angle and accentuates her beautiful eyes.  I can see you in her catchlights!</td>', 'A beautiful baby!  Her skin tones seem a bit cool to me.  Nice focus and the hood is very cute.  The light is coming from below her, which is not the most flattering way to light the face.  Next time try turning her around and shooting from above her head (so she has to look up at you) instead of standing at her feet.  It helps avoid that ''up the nose'' angle and accentuates her beautiful eyes.  I can see you in her catchlights!', '2006-04-17 16:41:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319637, 321907, 15204, '<td valign="top">Nice job finding a good natural setting.  The background works well.  He is underexposed and your white balance is off.  The shade is making his skin tone too cool.  A cutie!</td>', 'Nice job finding a good natural setting.  The background works well.  He is underexposed and your white balance is off.  The shade is making his skin tone too cool.  A cutie!', '2006-04-17 16:42:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2319645, 322016, 33515, '<td valign="top">Very soft focus, almost to soft.</td>', 'Very soft focus, almost to soft.', '2006-04-17 16:47:44.000000', NULL, 1),
