(2337925, 319424, 47117, '<td valign="top">Just to clarify, a lot has been said about the processing of this image. Little was actually done. It took me all of 10 minutes.  The only coloring added was to the green of his eyes to accent his natural color. The rest is all natural coloring using only a desk lamp, other than brightness/contast, yadda yadda, the basics. The processing to the face was actually minimal. A few distractions removed.  His face is really rather smooth and almost angelic, and that is why I used him. No neat image was used, no. The finger I left in because for me it added a bit of interest - a bit of his personality.  I liked the dimple it made in the cheek. He is very blushed because he just got done playing real hard before this pic was taken. <br/> <br/>Thanks to those that liked it along with me!! I see quite a few 5''s and 6''s and that is exactly what I thought I would find at challenge end. I am very happy with those and I am thrilled with the scores above that :)  For those that scored it lower, I understand your reasoning, and respect that.  This was just a shot I almost pulled, but left it in simply because I loved it.  The placement of it never really mattered.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Just to clarify, a lot has been said about the processing of this image. Little was actually done. It took me all of 10 minutes.  The only coloring added was to the green of his eyes to accent his natural color. The rest is all natural coloring using only a desk lamp, other than brightness/contast, yadda yadda, the basics. The processing to the face was actually minimal. A few distractions removed.  His face is really rather smooth and almost angelic, and that is why I used him. No neat image was used, no. The finger I left in because for me it added a bit of interest - a bit of his personality.  I liked the dimple it made in the cheek. He is very blushed because he just got done playing real hard before this pic was taken.  Thanks to those that liked it along with me!! I see quite a few 5''s and 6''s and that is exactly what I thought I would find at challenge end. I am very happy with those and I am thrilled with the scores above that :)  For those that scored it lower, I understand your reasoning, and respect that.  This was just a shot I almost pulled, but left it in simply because I loved it.  The placement of it never really mattered. ', '2006-04-24 01:19:11.000000', NULL, 0),
