(2338149, 321408, 34938, '<td valign="top">How on earth did this finish in 40th place??? this deserved at least top 10...you were robbed!</td>', 'How on earth did this finish in 40th place??? this deserved at least top 10...you were robbed!', '2006-04-24 02:14:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338151, 321328, 48228, '<td valign="top">MAGICAL....a wonderful vibrant portrait of a beautiful model.....<br/>You so deserved the "BLUE" for this stunning image.....<br/>CONGRATULATIONS.....</td>', 'MAGICAL....a wonderful vibrant portrait of a beautiful model.....You so deserved the "BLUE" for this stunning image.....CONGRATULATIONS.....', '2006-04-24 02:14:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338156, 321987, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by fotodude:</b></div><hr/><i> the post prosses here is very drastic and i can see the eadges, next time watch for that with feathering or blend it better in another way so it is less appearent. also using DoF to achieve the same resould would have saved time and been a cleaner image in the end.....its a nice cover also but doesn''t strike me as a studio portrait...this is based on the difused/and somewhat flat light (as from a cloudy day)... a spot simple home light set up and it would read more as studio... </i></td></tr></table> <br/>You are quite right on two points -- sloppy masking and an outdoors shot. I was rushed in my editing (shot the last day) and had zero indoor portraiture opportunities during the week. My camera will only achieve a shallow DOF on macros, hence my attempt to achieve it in post-processing.</td>', 'Originally posted by fotodude: the post prosses here is very drastic and i can see the eadges, next time watch for that with feathering or blend it better in another way so it is less appearent. also using DoF to achieve the same resould would have saved time and been a cleaner image in the end.....its a nice cover also but doesn''t strike me as a studio portrait...this is based on the difused/and somewhat flat light (as from a cloudy day)... a spot simple home light set up and it would read more as studio...  You are quite right on two points -- sloppy masking and an outdoors shot. I was rushed in my editing (shot the last day) and had zero indoor portraiture opportunities during the week. My camera will only achieve a shallow DOF on macros, hence my attempt to achieve it in post-processing.', '2006-04-24 02:16:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338158, 321359, 31133, '<td valign="top">Nice job, Deannda. I agree with the comments below both about the backdrop (for me, this is the only niggle) and the great lighting. Love how natural they both look. The colors of their shirts set off their faces - nice!!</td>', 'Nice job, Deannda. I agree with the comments below both about the backdrop (for me, this is the only niggle) and the great lighting. Love how natural they both look. The colors of their shirts set off their faces - nice!!', '2006-04-24 02:16:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338159, 321309, 47294, '<td valign="top">So I''m not even close hey!!!  Less than a point my friend...<br/> <br/>Congrats on your finish mate, great photo.</td>', 'So I''m not even close hey!!!  Less than a point my friend... Congrats on your finish mate, great photo.', '2006-04-24 02:17:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(2338162, 320965, 28742, '<td valign="top">This is awesome, Jason! Congratulations!</td>', 'This is awesome, Jason! Congratulations!', '2006-04-24 02:18:27.000000', NULL, 0),
