(2339520, 321726, 93, '<td valign="top">I''m going to throw something out there:<br/> <br/>I can understand the low votes. Especially the 1s.  (Doesn''t mean I necessarily *agree* with them fully).  <br/> <br/>There are a very many people on this site that hate feeling manipulated. That hate feeling like they''re being played for the fool.  There are also people on this site that view such things as the same model (especially one so recognizable), in consecutive or near consecutive challenges, violates the spirit of DPC.  This leads to emotions that lead to scores of 1, 2, or 3.<br/> <br/>Whether you agree with it or not, these people''s thoughts and reactions are here to stay and are a part of the site, and should be respected along with everything else.<br/> <br/>I''ve been a victim of putting the same model in too many challenges too closely together myself.  People simply don''t like it.  That''s the chance you take when you submit something of this nature, and I bet donuts to dollars that Manny knew this when he submitted.  <br/> <br/>Instead of being angry at the people that are angry at Manny, just enjoy the photo if you like it.<br/> <br/>Personally, and as much as I think Manny is a great guy, this *does* smack a little too much of voter manipulation... but hey.. it''s competition. It''s DPC.. and you do what you gotta do.  Some of us might not like it, but life goes on.</td>', 'I''m going to throw something out there: I can understand the low votes. Especially the 1s.  (Doesn''t mean I necessarily *agree* with them fully).   There are a very many people on this site that hate feeling manipulated. That hate feeling like they''re being played for the fool.  There are also people on this site that view such things as the same model (especially one so recognizable), in consecutive or near consecutive challenges, violates the spirit of DPC.  This leads to emotions that lead to scores of 1, 2, or 3. Whether you agree with it or not, these people''s thoughts and reactions are here to stay and are a part of the site, and should be respected along with everything else. I''ve been a victim of putting the same model in too many challenges too closely together myself.  People simply don''t like it.  That''s the chance you take when you submit something of this nature, and I bet donuts to dollars that Manny knew this when he submitted.   Instead of being angry at the people that are angry at Manny, just enjoy the photo if you like it. Personally, and as much as I think Manny is a great guy, this *does* smack a little too much of voter manipulation... but hey.. it''s competition. It''s DPC.. and you do what you gotta do.  Some of us might not like it, but life goes on.', '2006-04-24 15:00:45.000000', NULL, 0),
