(2340281, 321081, 22734, '<td valign="top">Hang in there. The comments pretty much spell out your lessons: You have a good eye for image and composition and all you need do is back off on the processing. Use these tools ever so lightly and you will be fine. Pretty girl.</td>', 'Hang in there. The comments pretty much spell out your lessons: You have a good eye for image and composition and all you need do is back off on the processing. Use these tools ever so lightly and you will be fine. Pretty girl.', '2006-04-24 21:26:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340291, 320581, 40718, '<td valign="top">You know, I''m having a bit of trouble deciding why this was a 5.1.  I think it''s a decent shot.  I gave it a 6.  Perhaps two things jump out at me.<br/> <br/>1) DPC does love a white background, but this is, if possible, too white.  It almost overwhelms you.  I don''t think gray would have been better, but instead of having a 0.0.0 white, maybe a 15,15,15 white or something would have been better.  I''m not sure.<br/> <br/>2) The pose is a bit static.  I think it''s a neat idea pulled off well.  Sure, it''s been done before, but not enough that it has become cliche.  I''m not a portrait artist, so I don''t have a lot to help you with the pose, but I wonder if that was part of the problem.<br/> <br/>3) I''m really puzzled by the 60 scores of 4.  I really don''t know.  Sometimes you win, I guess and sometimes you lose.  Keep it up though.</td>', 'You know, I''m having a bit of trouble deciding why this was a 5.1.  I think it''s a decent shot.  I gave it a 6.  Perhaps two things jump out at me. 1) DPC does love a white background, but this is, if possible, too white.  It almost overwhelms you.  I don''t think gray would have been better, but instead of having a 0.0.0 white, maybe a 15,15,15 white or something would have been better.  I''m not sure. 2) The pose is a bit static.  I think it''s a neat idea pulled off well.  Sure, it''s been done before, but not enough that it has become cliche.  I''m not a portrait artist, so I don''t have a lot to help you with the pose, but I wonder if that was part of the problem. 3) I''m really puzzled by the 60 scores of 4.  I really don''t know.  Sometimes you win, I guess and sometimes you lose.  Keep it up though.', '2006-04-24 21:33:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340311, 320903, 19672, '<td valign="top">I like this shot a lot...I really think it should have ranked higher.<br/> <br/>- Saj</td>', 'I like this shot a lot...I really think it should have ranked higher. - Saj', '2006-04-24 21:45:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340450, 321324, 27767, '<td valign="top">I absolutely love this crop; it gets nice and close for a really personal feel. I love that both eyes have catchlights and the shadows are not too harsh. The color of the hat couldn''t be better. It adds a great sassy splash to a technically immaculate shot.</td>', 'I absolutely love this crop; it gets nice and close for a really personal feel. I love that both eyes have catchlights and the shadows are not too harsh. The color of the hat couldn''t be better. It adds a great sassy splash to a technically immaculate shot.', '2006-04-24 22:57:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340473, 321483, 27767, '<td valign="top">For what it''s worth, I''d like to say that I really appreciate no frills approach to this shot. It particularly stands out against the other top 10 finishers in this challenge as having the least out of camera processing. I really admire the raw skill and forethought required to achieve this.</td>', 'For what it''s worth, I''d like to say that I really appreciate no frills approach to this shot. It particularly stands out against the other top 10 finishers in this challenge as having the least out of camera processing. I really admire the raw skill and forethought required to achieve this.', '2006-04-24 23:06:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340510, 321328, 43432, '<td valign="top">wow!</td>', 'wow!', '2006-04-24 23:24:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340599, 321376, 48928, '<td valign="top">I think this is waay underated.  That''s the voting on DPC.  I gave the 10 you got in the challenge, i think the only reason this may not have scored higher was in certain areas it seems slightly OOF.  The expression more then makes up for it to me though :)</td>', 'I think this is waay underated.  That''s the voting on DPC.  I gave the 10 you got in the challenge, i think the only reason this may not have scored higher was in certain areas it seems slightly OOF.  The expression more then makes up for it to me though :)', '2006-04-24 23:55:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340626, 321556, 42826, '<td valign="top">I thought you had a great shot!!  I wished it would have placed even higher!</td>', 'I thought you had a great shot!!  I wished it would have placed even higher!', '2006-04-25 00:02:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(2340793, 321875, 51802, '<td valign="top"><b>Hello from the Critique Club!</b> <br/> <br/>There are just a few things I see here that could use a little tweaking.  The lighting is what I think kept this photo from scoring higher.  The light on the her right side is too harsh.  I am assuming this is natural light coming in from a window.  It may have helped to partially close a shade, or position something in between her an the light to lessen it some.  Another option would be to lightly use the burn tool in post processing since this was an advanced editing challenge.  I like that you have two light sources and that they are not equal in strength.  The lighting on her left side is much softer and has a more comforting feel.  Adding some fill flash would help brighten up her eyes, which seem to be a little dark.  One final nit-pick would be the cropping.  The edge of the frame cuts out some of her hair.  This makes it feel cramped.  Allowing the background to completely surround her head would help with this.<br/> <br/>You had a few comments where people said you over sharpened.  I really think you did a nice job with this.  People''s eyes may have been drawn to her lips and chin, where the wrinkles are more pronounced, but looking at her cheeks tells me that this really is natural.  Another thing fill flash may have done is make the wrinkles a little less pronounced.<br/> <br/>Her pose is wonderful.  She seems quite relaxed and comfortable.  It makes me feel like she has just finished telling a story of one of her life experiences, and is now looking at me to make sure her point sinks in!<br/> <br/>-Bill<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club!  There are just a few things I see here that could use a little tweaking.  The lighting is what I think kept this photo from scoring higher.  The light on the her right side is too harsh.  I am assuming this is natural light coming in from a window.  It may have helped to partially close a shade, or position something in between her an the light to lessen it some.  Another option would be to lightly use the burn tool in post processing since this was an advanced editing challenge.  I like that you have two light sources and that they are not equal in strength.  The lighting on her left side is much softer and has a more comforting feel.  Adding some fill flash would help brighten up her eyes, which seem to be a little dark.  One final nit-pick would be the cropping.  The edge of the frame cuts out some of her hair.  This makes it feel cramped.  Allowing the background to completely surround her head would help with this. You had a few comments where people said you over sharpened.  I really think you did a nice job with this.  People''s eyes may have been drawn to her lips and chin, where the wrinkles are more pronounced, but looking at her cheeks tells me that this really is natural.  Another thing fill flash may have done is make the wrinkles a little less pronounced. Her pose is wonderful.  She seems quite relaxed and comfortable.  It makes me feel like she has just finished telling a story of one of her life experiences, and is now looking at me to make sure her point sinks in! -Bill', '2006-04-25 00:53:23.000000', NULL, 0),
